| Notes on particular styles:
|   LineNum wraps a single line number. LineNums wraps multiple
| paragraphs, clearing room on the left margin for the line
| numbering. See RNIB Braillist's Manual UEB Edition section 33.
| Note that [svlma:4] is really appropriate for two-digit line
| numbers, which we simply presume to be most common. Linear
| styles used within LineNums must use commands such as [hi]
| that honor left margin adjustment (parameter to [svlma]).
|   The TranscriberNote character style simply adds indicators
| before/after note text. When used to contain an explanatory
| note for a diagram, e.g., it should be used within a para.
| linear style to get the proper format. (See RNIB Braillists'
| Manual, UEB Edition, section 23.8.1.)
